I've replaced the hand-written Sonnet 4.6 row and the Bedrock limits stopgap with yoagent 0.26.7's presets. It's committed as f2553063. Build, the full test suite, clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check all pass.

Sonnet 4.6 (#1123). The anthropic_preset arm now calls ModelConfig::claude_sonnet_4_6(). Before deleting the old row I printed both versions field by field: every public field was identical, including window, max_tokens, reasoning, cost and the Anthropic compat flags. So the requests yoyo sends don't change. One field, `list_priced`, is private and couldn't be compared. The test that checks Anthropic's published figures stays, and now also asserts it equals yoagent's constructor. No "#1123" text is left anywhere in src/ or docs/.

Bedrock limits (#1124, limits half only). The bedrock arm now takes window, max_tokens and reasoning from ModelConfig::preset("bedrock", id). It doesn't copy yoagent's base URL, so the user's Region is kept.
• Cost: one change beyond the task. yoagent's Bedrock preset has no price, and the old arm had copied the Anthropic base price. That under-billed regional endpoints by 10% in the totals yoagent keeps itself, including sub-agent spend. The arm now uses the same Bedrock price rule /cost uses (bedrock_preset_cost, made pub(crate)), so those totals agree with /cost.
• Resolver comparison. I ran the old and new resolvers over 32 ids. They differ on 5, all shapes the old mapping accepted and yoagent refuses: an unknown xx. prefix, -v1:0 and -v2 suffixes, anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5, and us.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5-v1:0. AWS's model cards for Sonnet 4.6 and Opus 5.5 list neither those spellings nor the xx. prefix. For anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5 I'm relying on yoagent's note that it's another AWS endpoint's spelling of Haiku 4.5, not the one yoyo uses; I didn't check AWS's Haiku card. So I filed nothing upstream. Those ids now run on guessed limits (200K / 16K) and print a warning.
• The default doesn't warn. anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6 still resolves and gets no guessed-limits warning, and the au., jp. and us-gov. prefixes behave as before.

Tests. I changed one existing test, stated in the commit:
• bedrock_claude_ids_run_on_the_anthropic_preset now compares against yoagent's Bedrock preset and has new rows.
• us.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5-v1:0 moved from the expected-to-resolve rows to the near-misses.
• The near-miss check on cost changed from "has no price" to "has what /cost charges", because the old, looser lookup still prices the stray Claude-looking ids.

cost_prices_bedrock_claude_ids_by_endpoint is untouched and green. I also checked the new test catches a regression: pointing the arm at a bogus id made it fail by name, and I restored the code afterwards.

What's left:
• Pricing half of #1124. providers::bedrock_anthropic_preset_id stays, now documented as a lookup used only for prices. I commented the comparison table on #1124. That means stray ids get guessed limits but a real price until yoagent prices Bedrock ids or exposes the vendor id.
• Other edits: docs/src/configuration/models.md now lists yoagent's prefixes instead of the old mapping. ARCHITECTURE.md has a "superseded at 0.26.7" note. src/agent_builder.rs went from 4977 to 4974 lines.
